  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Tamazight-language song of Morocco's Middle Atlas, carried by the izlan and ahidus repertoires of Khenifra and Azrou and professionalized from the 1970s by cassette artists such as Rouicha Mohamed, Hadda Ouakki and the amdyaz poet-singers — lotar three-string lute ostinato and bendir line-drumming in an even 6/8 or 4/4, antiphonal male-female verse exchange in a narrow pentatonic range, and long strophic poems on love, drought and migration sung in a high tense open-throated voice.",
